thesis and boundary; this supplement gives the finite-record definitions, theorem proofs, and case-evidence tables; and the supplemental evidence directory
supplies only the finite records named in the bundle-dependent claims when
that exact support surface is uploaded with matching final digests. This file
records a compact workflow pattern for avoiding these failures: an auditable
theory-to-paper pipeline in which AI agents propose, review, and triage, while
deterministic gates decide what may be treated as load-bearing evidence. The
pattern is instantiated in local BEDC and automath workspaces. The mathematical content of the supplement is the explicit finite-record safety interface for
this workflow: definitions for gate vocabulary, a pinned imported theorem spine,
a constructive finite publication-certificate theorem, a current-package finiterecord certificate-exactness theorem, evidence-level and formal-source promotion
obstruction theorems, and witness records for the four required cases. The result
is intentionally not a proof of external implementation-level soundness: Lean
builds, publication-daemon behaviour, artifact semantics, and fresh command
runs enter the argument only when a finite certificate records the corresponding
evidence surface and boundary. Root-level diagnostic files outside the submitted
primary article, this supplement, and the uploaded-or-equivalent review bundle
are treated below only as local historical or path-verified context unless a displayed certificate explicitly places the corresponding record on the submitted
support surface. The CICM presentation-only submission uses the short artifact
plus bibliography; this supplement and review_bundle/ are evidence-support
materials rather than competing primary submissions.

