support surfaces. The opening package paragraph of this supplement names the
same four coordinates and explicitly selects exact supplemental inclusion rather
than an archive replacement. The digest manifest review_bundle/FINAL_DIGE
STS_SHA256.md records the same branch: its support mode is conditional exact
supplemental inclusion of review_bundle/, and its archive-replacement fields
state that no archive replacement or locator is claimed. These three finite source
records therefore agree on one package shape.
It remains only to identify the boundary of the convention. A source-level
package-shape record fixes which files the manuscript treats as primary, supplemental, and support material; it does not by itself prove that a venue upload has
occurred. Hence bundle-backed claims are admissible externally only after the
selected exact support directory is actually supplied with the digests listed in the
final manifest. If that external inclusion record is absent, the finite coordinates
still exist locally, but the submitted-support conclusion is not instantiated. Since
the same finite records contain no archive locator, no archive replacement can
be inferred from the source. This proves both the single package convention and
its conditional external boundary.
