We distinguish two evidence levels. A claim is path-verified when this paper
records the relevant source path, artifact path, pinned commit or local publication
path, and gate decision, but does not assert that a command was freshly rerun
for this submission. A claim is command-run when the paper also records the
command, source commit, environment, exit code, and log path for a fresh run.
This long technical supplement uses path-verified architecture and case evidence
unless explicitly marked command-run.
