It remains to prove that the displayed obstruction list is complete. Suppose
an accepted claim fails the publication-safety interface. Choose an inclusionminimal subrecord of its acceptance entry that still witnesses failure. The certificate schema has exactly seven coordinates, and the first two of them are not
extra obstruction families. The claim-kind coordinate K only determines the finite gate set G(c) through G ; once K lies in the seven-kind domain, any failure
caused by that determination is a missing assigned gate and hence type 2. The
evidence-level coordinate l only chooses between the path-verified and commandrun interpretations of the boundary field; its failures therefore appear either as
