Therefore the current package supports exactly the path-verified publication-safety
claim that its load-bearing case-study assertions are reviewable, gate-typed, and
equipped with locally checkable publication certificates at the path-verified level.
The corollary is historical and record-level: it instantiates the certificate constructor using the listed paths, tables, and bundle records, not by rerunning the
whole workflow. It does not instantiate any stronger claim that the full newmath
source tree, a publication daemon, an artifact validator, or the Rule110 dynamic
artifact suite was freshly rerun.
Proof. The package P contains exactly the submission-local source files and manifest records named in the statement. Lemma 1 shows that the source-interface
table is the complete imported interface used by this paper, and Propositions 3

