camera-ready approval, or proceedings publication.

Proof. The table has five rows, so the check is finite. The route-class row compares the venue’s presentation-only rule with the local role separation already
fixed by Proposition 1: submission_abstract.tex is primary, while main.tex,
theorem_inventory.json, and exact review_bundle/ inclusion are support artifacts. If the primary artifact is not the short source, if those support
artifacts are presented as a second primary proceedings paper, or if the bundle branch is silently changed to an unrecorded archive replacement, this row
fails. If it passes, the row proves only compatibility with the presentation-only
artifact split, because its boundary column expressly excludes acceptance and
proceedings-publication claims.
The formatting row is a syntactic source check. The manuscript begins with
the LNCS class llncs; the package uses splncs04 for the bibliography; and
the local compiled short artifact and bibliography files are present as submis
sion_abstract.pdf and submission_abstract.bbl. These are finite path
and token checks. They do not inspect Springer production systems, nor do
they prove that the venue will accept the formatting; hence the row gives local
formatting readiness only. The supplement-access row is finite because it requires
the selected exact bundle files, the final digest manifest, and the root theoreminventory coordinate named by the manifest and certificate ledger. Audit record 1
remains only the criterion that would have to be satisfied by a future archive
replacement; it is not the branch selected by the current source package. The
metadata and bibliography row checks the title, author block, institute/email
block, bibliography command, and references.bib; it does not certify external
metadata entry. The deadline row records only that the package can be checked
against the venue date before upload and does not assert that an upload was
made.
If all rows pass, each venue-facing submission claim used by this manuscript
has a finite witness and an explicit negative boundary, so the package is ready in
the limited local sense stated in the proposition. Conversely, if any row fails, one
of the finite route-class, formatting, supplement-access, metadata, bibliography,
or deadline witnesses required by the table is absent or stale; there is then no
local certificate for submission-pack readiness. The final sentence follows from the
boundary column and from Definition 2: external upload, acceptance, camera-

