2. Lean correctness, full-source rebuild success, or axiom-purity beyond the recorded
formal-source gate fields;
3. end-to-end external semantic validity of artifact data beyond the finite manifest and evaluator surfaces named in E and R;
4. a fresh daemon run, full-source rerun, Rule110 or GroundCompiler rerun, or
journal or workshop acceptance; or
5. bundle-backed reviewability when neither re vi ew _b un dl e/ nor an archival
equivalent carrying the same finite records is in the submitted artifact boundary.
More precisely, such a stronger reading has an inclusion-minimal bad subrecord
of one of the five types in Theorem 7. Hence the accepted claim is rigid at its declared evidence level: path-verified certificate records cannot be promoted by prose
into command-run evidence, semantic validation, formal-source correctness, or
external acceptance.
Proof. Let c+ be one of the stronger readings. It has the same displayed manuscript
