A command-run claim is outside the present evidence level unless the source
commit, environment, command, exit code, and log path are recorded with the
submission. This boundary is deliberate: the workflow is meant to make unsupported claims visible rather than to hide them behind generated prose.
For the current presentation-only submission route, the public source link is
the newmath repository [3] at pinned commit 3fb3d6a0641767388a401883062a
a522ea0b397b. The automath workspace record and the review-bundle record
are treated as submission-local support notes, not ordinary external bibliography items. They provide extracted line-range records, case-evidence manifests,
submission-local provenance, and the technical supplement only when uploaded
exactly with the submission and matching final digests, as required by Proposition 24. No DOI, institutional archive, dynamic validation service, or fresh
command-run evidence is claimed here; the bundle-dependent evidence claim is
conditional on that supplemental surface being available to reviewers.

7

Scope

This note does not claim that AI output is proof evidence, that the workflow
is a theorem prover, that all BEDC declarations have been freshly rebuilt, or
that the Rule110 artifact suite has been rerun for this submission. Its narrower
claim is that a theory-to-paper pipeline can preserve traceability by separating
source evidence, deterministic gates, agent suggestions, and human promotion
decisions.

